# DTF tier manifest: scan-iso-rootfs-inventory  (artifact-keeper 1.12.0, #1966)
# Profile-set: filesystem only. LOCAL-ONLY: the scan runs the backend image's
# bundled Grype with its pre-seeded DB and the bundled unsquashfs; the ISO
# fixtures are written at run time by fixtures/make_fixtures.py (stdlib
# Python, no xorriso or squashfs-tools on the runner), so nothing depends on
# the network.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS:
#   * An uploaded ISO9660 live medium was staged as one opaque file: Grype
#     cataloged nothing inside it, the scan stored 0 packages and the
#     repository graded A. Since #1966 the scanner locates the embedded
#     squashfs rootfs (live/filesystem.squashfs), extracts its package
#     database and grades it: the dpkg status names openssl
#     3.0.11-1~deb12u2, which is vulnerable on Debian 12.
#   * An ISO whose squashfs is corrupt read exactly as clean as an empty one.
#     Since #1966 the scan is recorded not_cataloged with a reason and
#     inventory_status 'partial', and flags the repository.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.7. Green: an image carrying #1966.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
